# GPU hang observed while probing the batch-size ceiling, 2026-08-07 ~18:49 UTC+3.
#
# This file is an OPERATIONAL OBSERVATION, not a measurement. The run died before it
# could write a CSV row, so no provenance header was ever emitted for it. What follows
# separates what was recorded, what is reconstructed from git history and the host, and
# what is unrecoverable. Nothing here should be read as pinned to a source state.
#
# --- RECORDED (captured in this file at the time, verbatim below) ---
#   * the preceding successful run's console line: q=3 n=24 gpu_hip M=1024,
#     310.956 matrices/s over 181 s, 55 shards, first quarter 311.298, last 310.738;
#   * the fault line emitted by the ROCm runtime;
#   * the ordering: M=1024 completed, then M=4096 was attempted and the process died;
#   * the post-fault rocm-smi row showing the device idle and cool again.
#
# --- RECONSTRUCTED (inferred after the fact; each with its basis) ---
#   * Source state: NONE EXISTS. The harness crate's first commit is 7540a821
#     (2026-08-07 19:09:46 +0300), about twenty minutes AFTER this fault, so the code
#     that hung was uncommitted working tree with no SHA to name. This is also why the
#     run has no header: source pinning was added later, in 5f195e84 (19:31:36), and
#     binary pinning later still, in d37d2f81 (21:16:41) - both introduced precisely
#     because runs like this one could not be tied to the code that produced them.
#   * Host: the same physical machine as every committed receipt, an AMD Ryzen 9 5900X
#     with an AMD Radeon RX 6950 XT (gfx1030). The CPU and GPU models are time-invariant
#     properties of the machine and can be asserted; the toolchain and driver versions
#     recorded in the committed receipts (rustc 1.97.0, ROCm 7.2.4, kernel 7.1.3-arch1-3)
#     were sampled hours later and are NOT evidence of what was installed at 18:49,
#     though no upgrade is known to have happened that day.
#   * Invocation: the `sustained` subcommand, from the console lines' shape. The 181 s
#     window is consistent with --seconds 180, but the flag itself was not logged, so
#     this is inference from the output, not a record of the command line.
#   * Seed: SEED_ROOT was a compile-time constant, 0xb488f02c00000001, unchanged across
#     the crate's history. The stream index the hung run drew from is NOT recoverable:
#     the pre-d37d2f81 allocator started every sustained run at the same base, and the
#     working-tree state that ran cannot be reproduced.
#
# --- UNKNOWN (unrecoverable; do not assert) ---
#   * binary_sha256 - the executable was never hashed and no longer exists;
#     harness_source_sha, deps_source_sha and the dirty flags - never captured;
#     the exact command line; the exact matrices drawn; rustc/ROCm/kernel at that moment;
#     the cause of the fault beyond the runtime's own "GPU Hang" string. In particular
#     nothing here attributes the hang to a watchdog timeout: that is one hypothesis
#     among others (driver defect, memory pressure, a transient), and no diagnostic was
#     captured that would separate them.
#
# The committed measurements all postdate this fault and were taken with binary
# b1fe566fe1d133f2cbd298d35ca5290707830b71e3670f891b9e86aa8978698c, built at harness
# source commit 0e0b0aec, after a full equivalence re-check passed. The study's section
# 4.5 states what this observation does and does not support.

sustained q=3 n=24 gpu_hip M=1024 ...
    310.956 matrices/s over 181 s (55 shards); first quarter 311.298, last 310.738
sustained q=3 n=24 gpu_hip M=4096 ...
HW Exception by GPU node-1 (Agent handle: 0x563ba2657af0) reason :GPU Hang

